WitOS has no Linux system call instruction contract: ABI-1 differs in numbers, statuses and results, so musl's inline ECALL stubs become calls into the system layer's dispatch (src/Substrate/libc), which maps each Linux call onto the kernel's (plan step V2.1, as S1.1 did for x86_64 and aarch64). VDSO_USEFUL stays: musl's riscv64 cache flush (src/linux/cache.c) asks __vdsosym for the vDSO's symbol first and takes the system call path when there is none, as on WitOS, where no auxiliary vector names a vDSO.

